# Switching on - the whole evening from the beginning
# The complete picture: from launching the program on the control computer to the state
# the room settles into. This is the file to read first, and the one to hold in your hand
# when you want to check the artwork against what it is supposed to do.
# Movement times are estimates; the counting times (appetites, blinking) are exact.

0 The program is launched on the control computer. Nothing moves: the bar, the two males and the three females stay exactly where they were left.
0.5 Every light on every body comes on at once - all five bodies lit together, for half a second.
0 They all go out again. This flash is deliberate: the electronics can wake up with random lights on, and this clears them. If a light stays on after this, that light is faulty.
0 The control page becomes available in a web browser. From here on the artwork does nothing at all on its own - it stays dark and still, for as long as you leave it, until a person presses start.
0 A person presses start.
-> starting-the-installation
0 Within about twelve seconds both males are turning and blinking, all three females are turning, and the bar is sliding end to end. The room goes from completely still to fully in motion in a few seconds, and stays that way.
240 Over the next four minutes every light slowly brightens as every appetite fills, until all five bodies are lit at full brightness and both males have settled into their "both appetites" blinking pattern.
0 From then on the picture no longer changes: five bodies turning back and forth, two rings blinking, one bar wandering end to end, all lights full. Encounters between a male and a female still happen, but they happen by coincidence and leave no trace - nothing on any body shows that one has taken place.
0 This is worth stating plainly, because it is the main gap between the artwork as it stands and the artwork as intended: a female recognising a male changes nothing. No light responds, no body stops, no appetite goes down. Everything you see after the first four minutes is the same loop repeating.
